**Why:** FairPlay requires the CBC family of schemes, so for a single CMAF endpoint serving FairPlay + Widevine + PlayReady together, `cbcs` is the cross-DRM default that all three can decrypt. A single CPIX document can't mix scheme values, and the scheme has to be compatible with every DRM system you're requesting keys for — `cbcs` is the one that satisfies FairPlay's hard requirement while Widevine and PlayReady both support it too.

For contrast, the other schemes won't work for this use case: `cenc` and `cbc1` are AES-CTR/CBC full-sample, and `cens` is CTR-based partial — none of those satisfy FairPlay's CBC-family requirement, so they'd break Apple device playback on a shared endpoint.", "type": "text"}], "created_at": null}

